# ArduCopter 4.7.2 SITL overrides on top of the pinned copter.parm, gazebo-iris.parm and the gimbal's
# parameters (loaded last, so these win). Names, values and units are those of ArduPilot git
# fb773567896014da007bca58358704d4a0d8516f: ArduCopter/Parameters.cpp, ArduCopter/events.cpp,
# ArduCopter/radio.cpp, ArduCopter/AP_Arming_Copter.cpp, libraries/RC_Channel/RC_Channels_VarInfo.h.
# docs/simulation.md, "Failsafes".
#
# The simulator has a radio the autopilot always sees, parked at roll, pitch and yaw 1500 us and
# throttle 1000 us (read from RC_CHANNELS while nothing was sent). MANUAL_CONTROL overrides it and
# the override ends 0.5 s after the last message, so the parked throttle returns. With the stock
# FS_THR_VALUE of 975 that is not a failsafe, and a Loiter copter descended at the full rate into
# the ground when the stream stopped (measured). The values below make it one.
#
# RC overrides (MANUAL_CONTROL is one) end this many seconds after the last one; the vehicle
# refreshes the fresh setpoint every 0.2 s. Default 3.
RC_OVERRIDE_TIME 0.5
# Radio failsafe: the throttle below FS_THR_VALUE (us, range 910-1100, default 975) for three samples.
# 1085 puts the parked 1000 us under it, and any MANUAL_CONTROL throttle from z 85 clear of it. The
# pre-arm check wants the throttle's minimum above FS_THR_VALUE + 10, so RC3_MIN is raised to 1100,
# and RC3_MAX lowered to 1900 to keep the middle of the stick, MANUAL_CONTROL z 500, at the middle of
# the throttle (hold altitude in AltHold and Loiter). The action, 7, is Brake or Land: Brake stops
# the copter and holds it for as long as the lease lives (Land only if there is no position
# estimate). Arming then needs the setpoint stream: the pre-arm check refuses a throttle below the
# failsafe value.
# The default RC_OPTIONS (bit 5) refuses to arm unless the throttle control input is zero, which the
# middle of the stick, the setpoint stream's neutral, is not. Clearing it leaves the pre-arm checks
# of roll, pitch and yaw (neutral) and of throttle too high in the manual-throttle modes.
RC_OPTIONS 0
RC3_MIN 1100
RC3_MAX 1900
FS_THR_VALUE 1085
FS_THR_ENABLE 7
# GCS failsafe (no heartbeat or MANUAL_CONTROL from MAV_GCS_SYSID 255, which is what a lost lease or
# a lost ground adapter looks like): 5 is Land. Timeout range 2-120 s, default 5. It lands what the
# brake was holding.
FS_GCS_ENABLE 5
FS_GCS_TIMEOUT 2
# Bits of what a failsafe leaves alone (Copter.h, FailsafeOption): 0 a mission in Auto, on the radio
# failsafe, 1 a mission in Auto, on the GCS failsafe (a mission flown out of reach, allow_missions:
# docs/real-vehicle.md), 2 a guided flight, 3 a landing, on the radio failsafe (so a guided takeoff or a
# landing needs no stick; the GCS failsafe still lands them). The default, 16, would skip the GCS
# failsafe in the pilot-controlled modes. 15 is bits 0 to 3; real mode with missions requires bits 0
# and 1 set (a lost link stops the sticks too) and bit 4 clear. Nothing but Auto is affected: Guided,
# Loiter and the stick modes land or brake as before.
FS_OPTIONS 15
# The geofence a mission out of reach relies on (AC_Fence.cpp, ArduPilot fb773567): on, with RTL or
# Land (1) on a breach. FENCE_ENABLE defaults to 0; FENCE_ACTION 1 is its default, set so that the
# value real mode requires is the one the simulation runs. The circle (FENCE_RADIUS 300 m) is the
# default, and the mission stays well inside it.
FENCE_ENABLE 1
FENCE_ACTION 1
# What real mode requires of a fence for missions: the maximum altitude and the circle (bits 0 and 1;
# no upload needed) and a ceiling of at most 120 m.
FENCE_TYPE 3
FENCE_ALT_MAX 100
# The battery failsafe real mode requires for missions (AP_BattMonitor_Params.cpp, ArduPilot fb773567):
# what ends a mission that runs long. 2 is RTL; the default, 0, does nothing. The simulated battery
# has no low-voltage threshold set (BATT_LOW_VOLT 0), so it never fires in the checks.
BATT_FS_LOW_ACT 2
# The gimbal. The simulator's radio parks channels 6 to 8 low, which the stock gimbal parameters read
# as roll, pitch and yaw at their limits (-30, -135 and -160 degrees): the camera looked up and back at
# its own mount (/gimbal/cmd_* read -30, +135 and -120 degrees at the joints). Neutral mode holds
# MNT1_NEUTRAL_* (degrees, body frame) instead: level in roll and yaw, pitched 20 degrees down, which keeps the horizon below the in-picture stamp.
MNT1_DEFLT_MODE 1
MNT1_NEUTRAL_X 0
MNT1_NEUTRAL_Y -20
MNT1_NEUTRAL_Z 0
